-a70d6d67becd","comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Box deploy SUCCEEDS after the fixes (2026-07-15): with Dockerfile ssh -V (#694), nginx map_hash_bucket_size (#694), and compose AWS_REGION (#696), the opcert image builds, compose-opcert-1 is Up on the rebar-gerrit box, the host nginx /opcert/ route loads, Gerrit stays HTTP 200 (unaffected), and the SigV4 round-trip completes verdict=PASS with a signed rebar.opcert.v1 DSSE envelope (job ca38092f). Full evidence on 76d2.","timestamp":1784082983806507001}],"created_at":1784080223711768001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ff875035-b6b0-43d9-9d61-a6c991039186","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"76d2-00c3-88e8-4654"},{"link_uuid":"e835d868-67d0-4023-b411-b5112660348f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d4fe-e36a-a8c3-4302"}],"description":"# op-cert deploy blockers (Dockerfile.opcert + nginx guard map)\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n1. Run the 76d2 box deploy on the Gerrit host (compose-up / `docker compose up -d --build opcert` + nginx render of rebar.conf.template).\n\n## Expected\nThe opcert container builds and the nginx /opcert/ route loads.\n\n## Actual\n- Docker build fails: `ssh-keygen -V` (validity-interval flag) errors -> empty version -> 'ERROR: OpenSSH >= 8.9 is required'.\n- nginx -t fails: 'could not build map_hash, you should increase map_hash_bucket_size: 64' (48-char guard token overflows default bucket).\n(Deploy fail-safe worked: nginx rolled back, Gerrit unaffected.)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert reads the OpenSSH version from `ssh -V` (not `ssh-keygen -V`); a test asserts this.\n- [ ] infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template sets `map_hash_bucket_size` before the guard map; a test asserts this.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the box deploy succeeds after the fix: opcert container up, nginx /opcert/ route loads, Gerrit unaffected.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51c